  "cover_link": "https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/marveldatabase/images/8/89/Strange_Tales_Vol_1_118.jpg",
  "plot_summary": "When viewing a replica of the planet Earth, the doctor sees a \"dark patch\" over the mountains of Bavaria.&nbsp; \"Supernatural forces are at work there!\"&nbsp; He must investigate!&nbsp; Soon, we see that a seemingly normal \"Herr Braun\" walks out of a quiet village before a \"mystic glow\" envelopes him, causing him to pay no further attention to others, even <i>after</i> he's stepped out of the glow.&nbsp; Soon, other villagers walk through this same area, and are likewise changed.&nbsp; The unaffected townspeople sense their village is under some sort of spell -- so many have been \"possessed\"!&nbsp; They feel as if they need to flee for their <i>lives</i>!\n\nDr. Strange soon arrives on the scene and learns of the situation from an aged, blind man, then goes to visit one of the \"possessed\" men.&nbsp; As Strange probes, something inside the man flees, leaving Strange with only the impression that he briefly sensed \"an evil, inhuman presence.\"&nbsp; That \"presence\" flies off unseen to warn the \"others\" of this newcomer with the different powers, one who is <i>not</i> just another weak human!&nbsp; It travels to another dimension to report but is given orders to return and take over this newcomer's mind and body.&nbsp; No one can prevent them from \"possessing the Earthlings!\"\n\nLater, when the creature returns to the \"dimension of the humans\" and tries to take over Strange's body, he finds it only an empty shell.&nbsp; Strange is in his ethereal form, which surprises the creature and leaves him open to be scanned by the sorcerer... and learn his \"darkest secrets.\"&nbsp; Sure enough, members of his race are from another dimension and are using this small village as a test to see if they can control it before moving on to the \"entire planet.\"\n\nAfter learning the truth, Strange abandons the creature, since there is nothing left to learn.&nbsp; To him, the only thing that matters is to find the place of concealment, and he leaves his hotel room without another thought.\n\nNow freed, however, the creature whose mind was probed, heads straight to his fellow invaders who have been possessing the inhabitants.&nbsp; They spread distrust of the \"accursed newcomer,\" and because the other townspeople have no idea who is possessed and who isn't, they are persuaded to band together against Dr. Strange.\n\nDoctor Strange soon learns that all the people have turned against him -- just as he's discovered the aliens' entry point.&nbsp; But the \"brainless rabble\" is no match against his skill, which allows him time to escape to the other dimension.&nbsp; There, he pits himself against one of the would-be invaders in a mystic \"struggle for supremacy between two champions from two completely different dimensions!\"\n\nDr. Strange ultimately overwhelms his opponent and commands the creatures to vacate the villagers at once and return home!&nbsp; They promise to never return to Earth, but just in case, Strange mystically seals shut the entrance between the worlds.&nbsp; They shall \"menace mankind no more!\"\n\nHe leaves the village, explaining nothing, leaving this incident to become one of their many legends to \"hand down from father to son! ... For the history of man is rich in legend... in folklore which is closer to the truth than any suspect!\"",
  "grade_one_liner": "Doctor Strange uncovers a sinister force corrupting an entire village.\nUnfortunately, the answer turns out to be a surprisingly ordinary invasion plot.",
  "subtitle": "When in Doubt, Invade Earth",
  "review_text": "[ASSET: left | MysteriousDarkPatch | width=12%] [ASSET: right | ProbeEvasion | width=12%] The situation that Doctor Strange faces is something he detects from afar, all thanks to the mystic globe scanner that he's apparently just unwrapped (perhaps a <i>present</i>?&nbsp; Maybe a gift from the Ancient One?&nbsp; [SPAN: fontsize=small; text=The text doesn't bother to say...]).\n[BR]\n[Br] By the middle of page 2, an otherwise ordinary-looking Bavaria farmer is scrutinized by the visiting sorcerer, the alien presence that has possessed him only <i>just evading</i> his mental probe.&nbsp; It hurries off to warn \"others\" of this newcomer!\n\nThe reader immediately senses that this story is somehow different from the ones that have preceded it (with the possible exception of Doc's origin tale), <i>especially</i> in that it is set here on Earth, far away from Tibet, the Ancient One, and at least so far, no hint of the presence of the dreaded [SPAN: severity=info; text=Baron Bored-o] [SPAN: fontsize=small; text=(copyright pending)].\n\n[SPAN: severity=success; fontsize=larger; text=At <i>last</i>, there is actual hope that Doctor Strange might prove himself a defender of Earth!]\n\nHow Strange detected the odd takeover of the Bavarian townspeople [SPAN: severity=error; text=is never really explained], other than to suggest he is able to detect dark forces at work in the mountains of Bavaria, all thanks to his \"earthly scanner\" (page 2), which for some reason has been \"sealed\" -- [SPAN: severity=info; text=until <i>now</i>, of course!]\n\nWhy Strange waited until this moment to break out this handy-dandy scanner is a mystery unto itself...\n\n<b>No</b>, what <i>is</i> important is that, by the end of page 4, the reader is alerted to an alien presence that is surreptitiously \"possessing the Earthlings!\"\n[ASSET: center | CamouflagedAliens | width=large]\n\nOne glance at these aliens <i>instantly</i> breaks the spell... and just like that...\n[BR] [SPAN: severity=info; text=we're back to the tired trope of some sort of other-dimensional beings sent to conquer Earth...]\n\n[SPAN: severity=warning; fontsize=larger; fonttype=bold-italic; text=Sigh...]&nbsp; [SPAN: fontsize=small; text=and it was going <i>so well</i>...]\n\n[DIVIDER]\n[ASSET: left | PlotIsDiscovered | width=13%] Even as the horrible memories of [LINK:1962:ST_103_torch0|ST #103|2026-05-01] and [LINK:1962:TTA_41_ant0|TTA #41|2026-05-01] began to resurface in my mind, I courageously took heart and [SPAN: severity=success; text=found within myself the wherewithal to turn the page...]\n[BR]\n[BR] But sadly, the <i>entire</i> second half of this 8-page tale became [SPAN: severity=info; text=little more than an obligation read].\n\nThe problem isn't that these events happen.\n[BR] [SPAN: severity=warning; text=It's that they happen with almost no mystery, suspense, or dramatic complication:]\n[HANG] * Dr. Strange learns what is really going on\n[HANG] * The alien creatures rile up the townspeople\n[HANG] * Strange escapes into the other dimension\n[HANG] * There is a terrific mental battle with the alien champion...\n[HANG] * ...which requires no punching or action panels whatsoever (thus sparing the artist the bother)\n[HANG] * Strange prevails [SPAN: fontsize=small; text=(what a <i>shocker</i>!)]\n[HANG] * the aliens flee their human hosts and skedaddle back home.\n[HANG] * Strange ensures they can never return\n[HANG] * and he leaves, never bothering to explain what happened\n\n[ASSET: left | MindVsMind | width=9%] [ASSET: right | OnTheRoadAgain | width=20%] <i>Yes</i>, the [SPAN: severity=success; fonttype=bold; text=day is saved], but the effort leaves Doctor Strange <i>alone</i> once again.\n[BR]\n[BR] The poor guy has no one outside of the Ancient One to share the heavy weight of his burden -- that of being the <b>mystic protector of Earth</b>.\n\n[BOTTOM_LINE]\nFar from being uplifted, I walked away from this story [SPAN: severity=error; text=mostly disappointed.]\n\n<i>True</i>, there was no mystic hand-waving or snake-like tendrils wending themselves around the title character while floating aimlessly through a strange realm, but...\n\n[SPAN: severity=info; text=Doctor Strange versus would-be alien invaders from another dimension...?]\n[BR] [SPAN: severity=warning; fontsize=larger; fonttype=bold-italic; text=Really?]&nbsp; That's what you got this month?\n[BR] What is this -- the 1950s again?&nbsp; Can we please be <i>done</i> with that??&nbsp; [SPAN: fontsize=small; fonttype=italic; text=(Please?)]\n\nTo say that there was nothing positive in the issue would be a lie.&nbsp; [SPAN: severity=success; text=I at least give the co-creators credit] for attempting to move the action (such as it was) away from the mystic realm and ground it on Earth.&nbsp; I believe that's what the strip needs, especially since Doctor Strange [SPAN: severity=warning; text=has no supporting cast,] which remains a genuine impediment.\n\nBut a story that started with actual promise (outside of the head-scratching unsealing of his nifty Earth-scanning device) instead ended with... [SPAN: severity=warning; fonttype=bold; text=aliens.]\n\n[HANG0] It was a mercifully short story that had [SPAN: severity=info; text=only a couple of crumbs of actual plot]\n[BR] [SPAN: fontsize=larger; text=-- and precious little reason to care what happened next.]",
  "highlight": "Armed with a new Earth-scanning globe, Doctor Strange investigates a Bavarian possession mystery and unearths a group of disappointingly familiar alien invaders."
}